==Restrictions==
Rarity: Only [[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal]] and [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare]]

==Battleground==
*5 [[Mr. Angel]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*1 [[Alpacky]] spawns after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Doremi]] spawns as the boss.
**5 [[Mr. Angel]]s spawn, delay 16.67~23.33 seconds<sup>500f~700f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn, delay 6.67~20 seconds<sup>200f~600f</sup>.
**1 [[Director Kurosawah]] spawns.

==Strategy==
The restriction dramatically upscales the stage's difficulty. Most Normal Cats fall easily to even Alpacky, let alone Doremi, practically forcing players to rely on whatever helpful Ubers they may own. Additionally, [[:Category:Legend Rare Cats|Legend Rare Cats]] are banned, meaning that potential carries such as [[Izanami of Dusk (Legend Rare Cat)|Izanami]] and [[Black Zeus (Legend Rare Cat)|Black Zeus]] are unusable. If that wasn't enough, the stage design can single-handedly invalidate many Ubers, and specifically obtaining the few viable ones is in itself a luck-based mission. [[Superfeline (Normal Cat)|True Superfeline]] is recommended for any Uberless strategy.

If you're fighting Doremi close to the enemy base and she wipes out your army, stop deploying cats and lure her close to the [[Cat Base]], away from Director Kurosawah, before sending anything out again.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]] - Greater Balrog works just as well as he did in [[Baby Fake (Merciless)|Baby Fake]] and can be used to melt almost any enemy with his extreme melee DPS. His low cost and recharge time enable him to be replaced quickly when lost, and stacking a few can potentially negate his vulnerabity to peons. Additionally, being Weaken-immune does improve his matchup against Mr. Angel.
*[[Issun Boshi (Uber Rare Cat)|Issun Boshi]] - In both forms, Issun Boshi is a specialist rusher whose Massive Damage ability meets quite a few targets here and deal bursts of damage to Doremi while wiping out the [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] and [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] peons with terrifying ease. It wouldn't carry the stage, but definitely makes said peons less of an issue.
*[[Maeda Keiji (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Keiji]] - Immortal Keiji at Level 43 with full Strengthen [[Talents|Talent]] investment and 2 Attack UP (Sm) [[Cat Combo|Combos]] will be able to deal enough damage to consistently juggle Doremi once strengthened, preferably behind the base as to avoid being weakened by Mr. Angel. If you wanted to use Keiji without Attack Combos, then Keiji needs to be at Level 50 with full Strengthen Talents and 2 levels in Attack Buff Talents. His resistance to [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] enemies also allows him to be useful when dealing with Kurosawah.
*[[Lasvoss (Uber Rare Cat)|Lasvoss Reborn]] - He is absolutely powerful, for a price, being that he is very reliant on his Savage Blow to truly be worth the gambit; at level 50 a Strengthened Savage Blow can heavily cripple Doremi to where you can simply chip her down and win without much hassle.
*[[D'arktanyan (Uber Rare Cat)|Valiant D'arktanyan]] - Similarly to Keiji, at Level 42 (with 2 S Attack Up combos), Valiant D'arktanyan is able to juggle Doremi but with less investment and setup. Since he has Long-Range, you'll have to make sure he gets knocked behind your base by Mr. Angel or Doremi to make sure that no enemies are able to stay in his blindspot, as shown in this [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JQ4f93dTJfo video].
*[[Shadow Gao (Uber Rare Cat)|Diabolic Gao]] - With enough damage to KB Doremi in a single hit, the ability to briefly freeze Traitless enemies and sporting high range and health, he's a powerful pick for this stage, but beware that his attack rate is rather long enough for Doremi to catch up; he's best when complemented by other units to help chip down Doremi.
*[[Kenshin Himura (Uber Rare Cat)|Kenshin Himura]] - A somewhat weaker alternative to Diabolic Gao if one doesn't own him, as he has a slightly longer attack cycle, lower range and less health, though his high damage is enough to make a contribution.
*[[Trixi the Merc (Uber Rare Cat)|Trixi the Revenant]] - With her rapid attacks against Doremi, she can easily clear out the peons and constantly freeze Doremi to prevent her from attacking. Her slow immunity and strong against abilities also allow her to tank some hits without being greatly affected. Although one should keep Kurosawah in mind when using her.
*[[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Ultra Kasa Jizo]] - Kasa Jizo's Ultra Form will dismantle this stage with some help from Research/Attack [[Cat Combo]]s and [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cat]] to dispatch the Alpacky. Spamming Jizo with these helpers wins the stage, no brainpower required.

==Trivia==
*Babies First is a pun on the saying ''ladies first''.
*Babies First and [[The Devil's Rhythm (Merciless)|The Devil's Rhythm]] are the only [[Restriction Stage]]s to allow [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cats]] but not [[:Category:Legend Rare Cats|Legend Rare Cats]].

